WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
Mother Teresa by Darcy Adrian Valance

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:12.130
Penguin readers level one, there are a lot of good people in the world, but not many

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:17.110
of them are world famous. Mother Teresa was a small

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.830
quiet nun. She died in 1997 in India,

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:27.490
but people in many countries remember her. They talk about

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.360
her and they love her. Why?

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:38.460
Read her story. The answer is here. Agnes Gonsha

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.890
For her 13 years, her name was not Teresa. It

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.140
was Agnes. Her family name was Boyaggio.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.070
There were two children in the family before her, a

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.530
boy and a girl. Then little Agnes Gonsha

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:02.240
came into the world on the 26th of August 1910.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.080
Her mother and father were from Albania,

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.010
but they lived in the town of Scopia. At that

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:16.970
time Scopia was in Serbia. They had a good home

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:21.870
because her father did well in his work. Then her

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:29.630
father suddenly died. Agnes was only eight years old. Her sister was 14 and her brother

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.510
was 11. Things were difficult for Agnes's

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:41.170
mother, but she was strong for her children. She worked and did well. She loved the children

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:45.990
and they had a happy home. There were some poor

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:53.050
people near their home. These people did not have much money for food and Agnes's mother was good

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.970
to them too. She was a Christian, a Catholic

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:02.390
and God was very important to her. She prayed to

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:10.350
God every evening with her children and they all went to church every week. At the church there

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.590
were stories about Christian missionaries in

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.640
India and poor African countries. These people lived for God.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:23.690
They went to India and Africa because they wanted to bring God's love to poor people

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:27.090
there. Some of the missionaries in India

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:34.510
were men from Scopia. Agnes loved hearing about the work of these missionaries. She started to

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.730
think, what am I going to do for God? She

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:43.510
wanted to live for God, but how? Did she want to be a

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.330
nun? Did she want to live only for God? She

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:53.950
prayed for answers. After five years the answer came to

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.610
her. She wanted to live only for him. She wanted

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:03.410
to be a nun in India. Her mother was very unhappy

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:10.430
about this. She loved her daughter and did not want to say goodbye to her. She went to her bedroom

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.990
and stayed there all day. But after a day and

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.270
a night she came out and said to Agnes, put your

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:24.450
hand in his hand and walk with him. On the

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:29.710
25th of September 1928 Agnes said goodbye to her friends

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.290
and her home in Scopia. At the station she said

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:39.450
goodbye to her family. She was 18 years old and she

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:45.310
did not see her mother or her sister again. To

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.520
India. She went by train and boat to Ireland.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.900
There she went to the home of the Loreto nuns.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.430
She wanted to be a Loreto nun because many of them

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:04.860
worked in India. Agnes stayed with the nuns at Loreto house in Dublin for six weeks.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:12.120
Then she was on a boat again to India. She was now sister Teresa.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:21.390
These days you can get from Ireland to India very quickly, but in those days people were on the boat

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:29.300
for seven weeks. It went from Ireland to Spain then across the Mediterranean Sea to Suez in Egypt

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:33.170
down the Red Sea across the Arabian Sea to Sri

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:36.100
Lanka and then up to Calcutta in India.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:45.200
From Calcutta she went by train to Darjeeling. Calcutta was a big place with a lot of noise

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:53.800
but Darjeeling was quiet and beautiful. Young sister Teresa did not know much English

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:59.110
but she was a good student. She was friendly too

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:03.440
and she often smiled. She was very happy there.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:11.640
After two years her English was good and she started to teach children in the nuns school.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.120
Then she moved to one of the Loreto nuns schools in Calcutta.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:22.560
Its name was Loreto Antali, a big school for girls.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.180
Many of the girls were from poor families.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:35.590
The school day started early in the morning but the nuns day started before that. Every morning

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:41.380
the nuns prayed for a long time. Then they worked in the school in the morning and the afternoon.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:49.420
They worked in the evening too because many of the girls lived at the school. After a long day

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:54.270
they prayed again and then went to bed. The nuns

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:58.010
did not have holidays. They did not listen to music

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:05.860
or go shopping. They did not see their families but they were happy because they lived for God.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:11.840
They were happy and strong all day because they remembered his love every morning.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.880
Sister Teresa liked teaching and she was good at it.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:21.960
She was a teacher at Loreto Antali for 12 years

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:28.040
and then from 1944 she was the head teacher for four years.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.080
The Streets of Calcutta

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:40.350
Calcutta or Calcutta today has 15 million people. In the

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:43.420
1940s it was a very big place too

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:48.850
and many new people arrived every year. The people were

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.090
Hindus, Muslims,

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:58.060
Christians, Sikhs and Buddhists. Calcutta had beautiful buildings, big hotels,

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:05.970
offices, banks and houses. Many writers and famous people lived there but

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:07.840
Calcutta had some big problems.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:14.860
A lot of people were very poor. They did not have any money and they lived in slons,

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:23.200
bad places with bad houses. Many people did not have a home. They lived and died in the streets.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:29.510
The years 1943 to 46 were very bad years for

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:33.650
Calcutta. There was not much food and it was very

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:41.490
expensive. Poor families did not have money for this expensive food and in those three years

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:47.900
about three million people died. Every day there were dead people in the streets.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:55.420
Mother Teresa wanted to help the poor people in the slums but this was difficult for her.

00:07:56.260 --> 00:08:03.050
She was a nun and nuns did not often go out into the streets. Many nuns helped poor people in

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:10.660
schools, big food kitchens and hospitals but nuns did not usually go out to poor people in slums.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:15.660
She prayed to God for an answer to her problem.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:21.390
On the 10th of September 1946 she was on a train

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:25.400
from Calcutta to Darjeeling and the answer came to her.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:34.190
The answer was go and work in the slums with the poor people. This was new work for a

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.930
nun and the head of the Catholic Church in

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:41.680
Calcutta said wait. He wanted to think about it first.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.220
Mother Teresa wanted to start quickly

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:51.290
but she waited two years. Then in August 1948 a

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:55.050
letter came from him. He was happy about her new

00:08:55.100 --> 00:09:00.910
work. Loreto Antaly was her home and the nuns were

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.830
her only friends but she said goodbye and moved

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:10.150
into a small room near a slum. The blue and

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:15.240
white sari. Indian women usually dress in saris.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:23.370
There are beautiful expensive saris and there are poor saris for poor women. Mother Teresa

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:28.840
dressed in a poor blue and white sari because she wanted to work with very poor people.

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:36.170
Today there are many nuns in these blue and white saris but on her first day in the slum

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:41.850
mother Teresa was alone. She was only one small woman

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:44.600
with no helpers and no money.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:53.640
How did she start her new work? First she prayed to God and then she walked into the slum.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:10:01.300
There she talked to poor children. Many of them lived in the street. They had no home,

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:07.750
no family and no school. She started to teach them

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:10.400
in the street. The children liked her

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:17.720
and the day after that a lot of children came to her new school. Then they came every day.

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:26.340
One day there was a poor old woman in the street. She did not have a home and she was very ill.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:33.830
The doctors in the hospital did not want her because she was poor and very old. She was a dying

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:38.300
woman. She did not have a family. She was alone.

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:41.840
People in the street did not want to go near her

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:46.020
but mother Teresa went to her and talked to her.

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:48.660
She washed the woman and stayed with her.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:56.570
The woman died but she did not die alone. She died with a friend with her hand in mother

00:10:56.620 --> 00:11:01.220
Teresa's hand. There were often dying people in those streets.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:03.900
Mother Teresa stayed with them

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:10.460
and they did not die alone. Many poor street people did not have any food.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:18.610
Mother Teresa asked people for food for them. Some people helped her. Some people were angry

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:23.710
and did not help. For two months Mother Teresa worked

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.960
alone. It was a difficult time for her.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:33.120
Then two of her Indian students from Loretta and Tali came to her and worked with her.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:41.530
After two years there were 12 nuns with her. They all had blue and white saris and they had

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:48.960
a name, the missionaries of charity. They worked in street schools and the open street clinics.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:55.400
These clinics were not hospitals but they were a big help for people in the slums.

00:11:57.080 --> 00:12:01.720
People in Calcutta started to talk about Mother Teresa and her missionaries of charity.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:06.760
Many people wanted to help her and to give money to her.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:15.530
In 1952 the government of Calcutta gave her a big building and she started a home for dying

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:20.690
people there. After this the nuns started a big home

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:27.460
for children. Many poor children in Calcutta did not have a home or a mother or father.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:36.310
At the nun's new children's home there was food and a bed for them and love too. For 10

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:39.540
years Mother Teresa and her missionaries of charity

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:44.720
worked only in Calcutta. Every year there were new nuns.

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:52.670
After 10 years they started to work away from Calcutta too. They opened new homes for dying

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.520
people, homes for children,

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:59.740
schools, clinics and food kitchens in 23 places in India.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:07.620
A love letter to the world. There are poor people in every country.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:13.720
In 1965 the missionaries of charity started working in Venezuela,

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:20.570
South America. After that they opened a home in Rome. Then they went to

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.940
Tanzania and many countries in Africa,

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:30.390
Europe and Asia. In 1969 there was a television program

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:32.640
about Mother Teresa and her work.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:36.770
It was a BBC programme and it was on British

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:41.250
TV first. After the programme many letters

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:46.760
arrived for her. A lot of people wanted to work with her or give money.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:54.950
Then people in Europe, the US and Asia watch the programme. People in many countries wanted to

00:13:55.000 --> 00:14:01.950
help her. Suddenly Mother Teresa was world famous. She did

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:11.230
not like being famous. The

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:15.320
she often said and she is sending a love letter to the world.

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:20.920
People often asked her about her work. One question was

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:25.560
you are with ill people and dying people every day.

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:28.940
Is it difficult? How do you do it?

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:35.530
Her answer was I see God in every person. For

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:39.140
Mother Teresa, love of God was the important thing.

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:45.960
She wanted to give her love to God but we cannot see God. We can only see God in people.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:50.670
She loved poor people and dying people because she loved

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:54.020
God in them. For her this was beautiful,

00:14:54.800 --> 00:15:01.830
not difficult. She was on television again in 1979 because

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.780
the Nobel Peace Prize went to her.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:11.140
This famous prize was $150,000 in that year. A lot of money then.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:16.400
Every year the prize goes to an important worker for world peace.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:22.160
Many important people go to Oslo from many countries for the prize day.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:28.290
On that day in 1979, Mother Teresa talked to them

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:32.100
about love and peace. They asked her,

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:39.060
how can we get world peace? She answered, go home and love your family.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:46.160
In the 1980s there were missionaries of charity in a hundred countries.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:52.540
They were not only in poor countries. There was a home for dying people in New York too.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:57.740
Mother Teresa often talked to heads of government in these countries

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:03.250
but she always dressed in her poor woman's sari. In

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:07.930
1990, Mother Teresa was 80 years old but she

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:11.970
did not start working. Her day started at four o

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:15.010
'clock in the morning. She worked all day and

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:21.090
into the night. She had little sleep. A light in

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:25.920
a dark time. Mother Teresa died in September

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:30.450
1997 at the home of the missionaries of charity in

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:35.110
Calcutta. At that time there were 4,000 missionaries

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:40.570
of charity in 123 countries and 3 million people worked

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:44.750
with them. People wanted to see her and say

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:50.920
goodbye to her. Poor people from Calcutta and people from the government of India came.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:57.490
Important people arrived from many countries. One person said about

00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:01.180
her. She was a light in a dark time.

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:05.910
Mother Teresa was a light for the poor people of

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:09.620
Calcutta but she is a light for all of us too

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:11.920
in every country of the world.
